{
  "name": "LexHive Lead Intake Production",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Why event_id shows up everywhere in this workflow\nThe React app already generates one `event_id` per visitor and sends it in the webhook payload. Every node below just carries that same ID forward — to Meta's API, and to the Airtable row.\n\nThat's the entire deduplication mechanism: Meta sees a browser Pixel event and a server CAPI event with the *same* event_id and counts them as ONE lead, not two. If we generated a new ID here instead, every lead would get double-counted.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 320
      },
      "id": "9540d798-5488-42aa-9465-bea55f8745db",
      "name": "Note - event_id dedup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -80,
        16
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Why Upsert, not Insert\nMatched on `event_id`. If n8n or the browser ever retries this webhook (flaky network, timeout), this node overwrites the same Airtable row instead of creating a second lead.\n\nThis is what makes a retry safe: worst case a row gets written twice with identical data, never duplicated.",
        "height": 220,
        "width": 300
      },
      "id": "9e2493c9-83e4-46e6-9a24-75fc7f3ce35f",
      "name": "Note - upsert safety",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        880,
        16
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "lead-intake",
        "responseMode": "responseNode",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "6152bd18-4c60-4249-9d89-8280f91147c6",
      "name": "Lead Webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -80,
        336
      ],
      "webhookId": "lexhive-lead-intake"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "// The only hand-written code in this workflow. Everything else uses n8n's\n// built-in nodes so the logic stays visible/inspectable without reading code.\n//\n// WHY this step exists: Meta's Conversions API requires email/phone/name to\n// arrive as lowercase, trimmed, SHA-256 hashes - never plain text. Hashing\n// happens here, once, right after the lead lands, so no raw PII travels\n// further than it has to. This is also the last point where the raw request\n// headers (for client_ip_address) are still available, before the item gets\n// reshaped down to just the body fields.\nconst crypto = require('crypto');\n\nconst body = $json.body ?? $json;\nconst headers = $json.headers ?? {};\n\nconst email = (body.contact?.email || '').toLowerCase().trim();\nconst phone = (body.contact?.phone || '').replace(/[^0-9]/g, '');\n\nconst fullName = (body.contact?.name || '').trim().toLowerCase();\nconst [firstName = '', ...rest] = fullName.split(/\\s+/);\nconst lastName = rest.join(' ');\n\n// Prefer a real upstream-proxy IP header over x-forwarded-for's leftmost\n// (client) entry, since x-forwarded-for can be spoofed by the client itself\n// if no trusted proxy strips/overwrites it first.\nconst clientIp =\n  headers['cf-connecting-ip'] ||\n  headers['x-real-ip'] ||\n  (headers['x-forwarded-for'] || '').split(',')[0].trim() ||\n  undefined;\n\nreturn {\n  ...body,\n  hashedEmail: crypto.createHash('sha256').update(email).digest('hex'),\n  hashedPhone: crypto.createHash('sha256').update(phone).digest('hex'),\n  hashedFirstName: firstName ? crypto.createHash('sha256').update(firstName).digest('hex') : undefined,\n  hashedLastName: lastName ? crypto.createHash('sha256').update(lastName).digest('hex') : undefined,\n  clientIp,\n};"
      },
      "id": "05256703-abc5-443f-9350-1cdf9c42656c",
      "name": "Normalize + Hash PII",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        160,
        336
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://graph.facebook.com/v19.0/2162676567929174/events",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpQueryAuth",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ data: [ { event_name: \"Lead\", event_time: Math.floor(new Date($json.submitted_at).getTime() / 1000), event_id: $json.event_id, action_source: \"website\", event_source_url: $json.tracking.page_url, user_data: { em: [$json.hashedEmail], ph: [$json.hashedPhone], fn: $json.hashedFirstName ? [$json.hashedFirstName] : undefined, ln: $json.hashedLastName ? [$json.hashedLastName] : undefined, fbp: $json.tracking.fbp || undefined, fbc: $json.tracking.fbc || undefined, client_ip_address: $json.clientIp || undefined, client_user_agent: $json.tracking.user_agent }, custom_data: { runs_ads: $json.answers.runs_ads, monthly_budget: $json.answers.monthly_budget, urgency: $json.answers.urgency } } ] }) }}\n",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "5b9fe539-2f84-468a-bb08-5ee37e88f3f7",
